// The host services a plugin may call while one of its callbacks runs.
//
// Deliberately small: logging and reading the invocation context the host
// already prepared. Everything that reads or changes the world is a command
// the host admits and applies through an existing game owner, so no import here
// may take a world lock, wait for a chunk, or block on I/O.
interface host {
    use types.{log-level};

    /// One diagnostic line. The host truncates long messages and rate-limits a
    /// plugin that logs too much; a guest must not rely on a line being kept.
    log: func(level: log-level, message: string);

    /// The plugin id the host bound to this instance. Present for correlation
    /// and for reading its own configuration; it grants nothing.
    plugin-id: func() -> string;

    /// Hash one password with Argon2id and return its PHC string.
    ///
    /// Synchronous and host-local: it runs the platform KDF inside the call
    /// and returns the encoded hash, never logging its argument. Refused in
    /// hook phases, like every other effect import.
    password-hash: func(password: string) -> string;

    /// Check one password against its stored PHC hash.
    ///
    /// Synchronous and host-local, with the same phase and logging rules as
    /// `password-hash`. A malformed hash verifies as false, never as an error.
    password-verify: func(password: string, phc: string) -> bool;
}
